{"ts": "2026-10-18T10:54:46+00:00", "event": "forecast", "slug": "2026-10-18-mc43326-which-party-hold-most-seats-us-house", "version": 1, "source": "metaculus", "post_id": 43326, "type": "multiple_choice", "median": 0.9, "iqr": [0.86, 0.93], "distribution": {"probabilities": {"Democrats": 0.9, "Republicans": 0.095, "Other": 0.005}}, "community": {"cp": null, "pro": null, "gold": null, "n_forecasters": null}, "thesis": "Midterm penalty for the president's party, a 5-11 point Democratic generic-ballot lead and a razor-thin starting majority put Democratic control near 90%, matching Kalshi and Polymarket at 90-92%. Most sensitive to a late generic-ballot reversal; Other (a tie) is negligible.", "mode": "initial"}
