{"ts": "2026-10-19T00:44:00+00:00", "event": "forecast", "slug": "2026-10-19-mc46124-annualized-real-gdp-growth-bea-report-its", "version": 1, "source": "metaculus", "post_id": 46124, "type": "discrete", "median": 3.3, "iqr": [2.7, 3.85], "distribution": {"percentiles": {"5": 1.5, "10": 2.0, "25": 2.7, "50": 3.3, "75": 3.85, "90": 4.5, "95": 5.0}}, "community": {"cp": null, "pro": null, "gold": null, "n_forecasters": null}, "thesis": "GDPNow sits at 3.6% (Oct 15), and Polymarket and Kalshi put about 65-70% on a print of 3.0% or more, which centres the advance estimate near 3.3% once GDPNow's usual overshoot is allowed for. The tails are wide because the nowcast rests on a large inventory build (+1.9pp) offset by a large net-export drag (-2.7pp), and the Q2 advance print missed its nowcasts by more than 1pp.", "mode": "initial"}
