{"ts": "2026-10-19T00:44:04+00:00", "event": "forecast", "slug": "2026-10-19-mc46125-its-october-30-2026-meeting-fda-dermatologic", "version": 1, "source": "metaculus", "post_id": 46125, "type": "binary", "median": 0.62, "iqr": [0.5, 0.72], "community": {"cp": null, "pro": null, "gold": null, "n_forecasters": null}, "thesis": "Advisory committees side with sponsors about 60% of the time, but less often after an FDA rejection. Here the rejection is efficacy-only, the trial met its primary endpoint with a clean safety profile, clinical consensus is pro-atropine, and the panel was convened through the sponsor's formal dispute, which tilts a benefit-risk vote toward YES. The forecast is most sensitive to how harshly the FDA briefing frames the modest 0.01% effect and the missing axial-length data.", "mode": "initial"}
